 "intro": [
  "More families of Judah, gathered from old records (\"these names are from ancient records,\" 4:22), then Simeon, whose towns lay inside Judah's territory and who were absorbed into it (Joshua 19:1). Many short lists here are not tied to the main line; a dashed line marks a family whose link is not given.",
  "The best-known name is Jabez, whose prayer (4:9–10) is the only story in the chapter."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Babylonian Talmud, Temurah 16a and Megillah 13a; Targum on Chronicles. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries (Japhet; Williamson; Knoppers).",
